1489:     \label{fig:results_stage1_errors}
1490: \end{figure}
1491: 
1492: LSTM also benefits from explicit time, with reductions in both error types. For CNN, however, the effect is mixed: the selected operating point improves, while PR-AUC declines and FN rises. This disagreement is informative. Thresholded F1 characterises one decision point, whereas PR-AUC evaluates ranking over thresholds. Timing is therefore not beneficial merely because it is present; its representation within the encoder matters, and an appended interval feature is not equivalent to an elapsed-time sequence coordinate.
