1532: Removing the tiled vector in Scheme~B raises macro-F1 by 1.30 percentage points and PR-AUC by 2.38 points over Scheme~A, although Scheme~A retains a small macro-precision advantage. Repetition of one aggregate vector at every position may therefore interfere with distinctions among packet tokens. Scheme~C strengthens this interpretation: flow statistics appear more useful when encoded through a dedicated pathway than when copied into each packet position.
