1534: Scheme~C is strongest overall, with macro-F1 $0.8954$, PR-AUC $0.8763$, 267 FP, and 293 FN. Both error counts improve over packet-only Scheme~B, indicating that aggregate statistics add information when they condition rather than replace packet evidence. Attribution must nevertheless remain at the level of the integrated design. Scheme~C introduces both extra parameters and a separate statistical pathway, so the present ablation cannot assign the entire gain specifically to token-FiLM. A parameter-matched concatenation control would be needed for that narrower claim.
