1337: \subsection{Checkpoint and Decision-Threshold Selection}
1338: \label{subsubsec:experimental_thresholding}
1339: 
1340: Checkpoint and decision-threshold selection are separate operations applied uniformly across experiments. First, the checkpoint with the highest validation PR-AUC is restored. Validation predictions from that checkpoint then determine the class-1 threshold:
1341: \begin{equation}
1342:     \delta^{*}
1343:     =\arg\max_{\delta\in\Delta}
1344:       F_{1,1}^{\mathrm{val}}(\delta).
1345:     \label{eq:validation_threshold_selection}
1346: \end{equation}
1347: In Stage~1, $\Delta$ contains thresholds induced by the validation precision--recall curve; Stage~2 searches 199 equally spaced values between 0.01 and 0.99. Once selected, $\delta^{*}$ is fixed and transferred to the test partition without adjustment. Test observations play no role in checkpoint, threshold, or hyperparameter selection.
